              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Fletcher, the Federal Circuit generally has exclusive jurisdiction to review MSPB decisions, but Section\u202f7703(b)(2) creates an exception that sends mixed cases to district courts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Christopher Landau",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 62,
              "start": 62
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Whether the Board\u2019s decision on the merits of a civil service claim determines jurisdiction is irrelevant; jurisdiction depends on the nature of the allegations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Christopher Landau",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case also raises whether an employee must exhaust administrative remedies before seeking district\u2011court review."
      }
    ],
