              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christopher Landau, when the Board rejects an employee\u2019s allegations about a civil\u2011service action, it makes a substantive merits decision, which does not determine jurisdiction."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Christopher Landau",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Christopher Landau, exhaustion is a defense; if the Board\u2019s decision is affirmed, there is a question whether the discrimination claim has been exhausted."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Landau",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 62,
                "start": 62
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Landau, jurisdiction over a mixed question turns on the allegations, not merely on the outcome of the civil\u2011service action."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner (Anthony W. Perry) \u2013 Arguments",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 28,
                "start": 28
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Fletcher, the Federal Circuit generally has exclusive jurisdiction to review MSPB decisions, but Section\u202f7703(b)(2) sends mixed cases to district courts."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 40,
                "start": 40
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Fletcher, employees have a right to a de\u202fnovo trial on discrimination claims, which cannot be obtained in the Federal Circuit."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Fletcher, a tolling rule is needed to determine which forum the employee should use for the discrimination claim."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 58,
                "start": 58
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Fletcher, if an employee does not seek review of the Board\u2019s decision, they may proceed directly to district court after exhausting administrative processes."
        }
      ],
